================================================================================
PART 10: SUMMARY AND KEY TAKEAWAYS
================================================================================

WHAT YOU'VE LEARNED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

✓ HTML forms have native submission behavior

✓ React can intercept submit events

✓ onSubmit belongs on the form

✓ type="submit" triggers form submission

✓ preventDefault() can cancel the native submit action

✓ Application code continues after preventDefault()

✓ Controlled form state remains available to the handler

✓ Validation can run before application-level submission

✓ Async API logic can follow successful validation

✓ Loading state can prevent repeat submissions

✓ Reset and submit are different form behaviors

✓ preventDefault() and stopPropagation() solve different problems

✓ Non-submit buttons inside forms should usually use type="button"

✓ Native browser validation and application validation are separate concepts


================================================================================
CRITICAL preventDefault() POINTS
================================================================================

• FORM HANDLER:

<form
  onSubmit={handleSubmit}
>


• SUBMIT BUTTON:

<button type="submit">
  Submit
</button>


• SUBMIT HANDLER:

const handleSubmit = (
  event
) => {

  event.preventDefault()

  // Application logic
}


• preventDefault()

Means:

"Cancel this event's default browser action."


• It does NOT mean:

"Cancel the event completely."


• It does NOT automatically:

Validate
Send API request
Update state
Reset form
Stop propagation


================================================================================
preventDefault() PATTERN
================================================================================

1. USER SUBMITS FORM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

<form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>


        ↓


2. HANDLER RECEIVES EVENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const handleSubmit = (
  event
) => {


        ↓


3. PREVENT NATIVE SUBMISSION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

event.preventDefault()


        ↓


4. VALIDATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const errors =
  validateForm()


        ↓


5. INVALID?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

YES
 ↓
setErrors(errors)
 ↓
Render Errors


NO
 ↓


6. PROCESS DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

await submitForm(formData)


        ↓


7. UPDATE UI
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Success
Error
Loading
Reset


================================================================================
preventDefault() VS stopPropagation()
================================================================================

preventDefault()
      ↓
Stops Browser's Default Action


stopPropagation()
      ↓
Stops Event Propagation


Example:

FORM SUBMISSION:

preventDefault()


NESTED CLICK EVENT:

stopPropagation()


Both can be used together only when both behaviors genuinely need to be
controlled.


================================================================================
KEY DIFFERENCES TABLE
================================================================================

+----------------------+--------------------------+----------------------------+
| AREA                 | NATIVE FORM SUBMIT       | CUSTOM HANDLER             |
+----------------------+--------------------------+----------------------------+
| Native action        | Runs                     | Can be prevented           |
| Browser navigation   | May occur                | App decides                |
| React validation     | Optional                 | Can be performed           |
| React state          | Depends on navigation    | Remains in current app     |
| API processing       | Browser/server workflow  | JS/application workflow    |
| UI feedback          | Server/new page possible | React can render it        |
+----------------------+--------------------------+----------------------------+


