================================================================================
KEY TAKEAWAY
================================================================================

The central React form pattern is:

<form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>

        ↓

const handleSubmit = (
  event
) => {

  event.preventDefault()

  // Validate
  // Process
  // Update UI
}


preventDefault() itself has one focused responsibility:

CANCEL THE EVENT'S DEFAULT BROWSER ACTION.


Everything after that:

• Validation
• API calls
• Success state
• Error state
• Resets
• Navigation

is application logic that YOU define.


